  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 304 AM EDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nThursday - Sunday...\n\nA upper level low pressure system near the west coast will merge \nwith the remnants of Hurricane Polo, and continue to move toward the \nCentral Plains. On Thursday, this system will lift into the northern \njet stream leaving a shortwave trough to the west of the Ohio \nValley. Additionally, a shortwave disturbance over the Great Lakes \nregion will interact with the ridging. Rain showers will return to \nthe area late Thursday into Friday as a cold front pushes toward the \nregion and moisture is advected into the region. Rainfall amounts \nacross the area are expected to range from 1-1.5\", with possible \nlocalized high amounts. At this time no severe threats are expected \nas guidance has instability very low and marginal shear. Rain \nchances will continue through the weekend, although confidence is \nlow due to disagreement in guidance. Depending on the movement of \nthe front will depend on the time that a post frontal area of \nsurface high builds in. If the cold front moves through the area \nslower than rain showers could linger through the weekend. Other \nguidance indicates that the front will push through and high \npressure will take over by late Saturday. A relief in temperatures \nback into the mid to upper 70s are also expected post frontal \nboundary.",
